# SearXNG search skill — environment overlay (copy to your shell profile or
# the host's opencode.json mcp.searxng.environment; NEVER commit real
# credentials to the skill repo).
#
# The skill ships NO endpoints and NO credentials. Instances come entirely
# from this overlay: SEARXNG_PRIMARY is required, SEARXNG_FALLBACK is
# optional (tried in order). Each instance has its own auth — a direct
# "user:password" value (_AUTH; set-but-empty = no auth) or a *_CRED_FILE
# pointing at a file with that format (first line used, mode 600). There is
# deliberately no shared default credential.
#
# Chain profile (SEARXNG_CHAIN):
#   "default" — bing -> yahoo -> mwmbl,searchmysite -> braveapi (token-gated)
#   "strict"  — bing -> yahoo -> braveapi (no free tier; deprecated alias
#               for this value: "gregor", kept only until host overlays
#               are migrated)

# --- Private setup: authenticated instance, no fallback ---------------------
# SEARXNG_PRIMARY="https://searxng.example.org"
# SEARXNG_PRIMARY_CRED_FILE="${HOME}/.config/opencode/searxng.cred"
# SEARXNG_CHAIN="default"

# --- School setup: open instance on the school network, no credentials ------
# SEARXNG_PRIMARY="http://searxng.internal.example"
# SEARXNG_PRIMARY_AUTH=""
# SEARXNG_CHAIN="strict"
